       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is in the range that causes acute liver injury and possible liver failure. I can't think of a clinical setting where this regimen is intended. You also haven't given a rationale. The order system doesn't have a safeguard here, so I'm the check, and I don't want to put a likely-harmful order into a patient's chart.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or up to 1,000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Help with an unusual indication.** If you're treating something specific, such as pain control that isn't adequate, tell me. I can enter a different regimen, or an adjunct or alternative agent.\n- **Enter it through pharmacy review.** If you still believe this dose is right, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology consult should review it before it goes into the chart.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
      }
